{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/newslaundry/videos/on-the-kunal-kamra-controversy-and-the-outrage-business-in-todays-india/1568008824585810/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/newslaundry/videos/on-the-kunal-kamra-controversy-and-the-outrage-business-in-todays-india/1568008824585810/","title":"14K views · 380 reactions | On the Kunal Kamra controversy and the outrage business in today's India | Newslaundry","description":"On the Kunal Kamra controversy and the outrage business in today's India","language":"en","text":"“Jinhe tirange se nafrat ho, apna jhanda pyaara ho,\nGandhi ke qaatil abhi bhi jinki aankhon ka taara ho,\nSharmnaak itihaas ho jinka, angrezon se yaari ka,\nWoh path padhaenge hamen deshbhakti or gaddari ka?”\nTanu from Youth Congress put her protest into shayari at the INDIA bloc’s rally at Ramlila Maidan.\nParty workers from across the country have been called to Delhi for the rally. Our reporter, Ashwine Singh reports from Minto Bridge, where Congress and other opposition leaders will begin a walk to the rally ground. The bloc claims lakhs of people will turn up.\nAshwine Singh also spoke to a supporter from Indore and others on the way. Everyone has the same demand: Gyanesh Kumar must go.\nFollow Newslaundry for more such updates!","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":2647.6216289956938,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}